Here are some suggestions for changes I think should be made to the
list of valid race/class combinations in Slash'EM.  Many thanks to
Dylan for helping to thrash out the list.  For those who don't play
Slash'EM, the current list of valid combinations is at
http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/races.html, and the
following changes have already been RFEd:

* Hobbit Flame Mages, Ice Mages and Wizards should not be allowed
  because hobbits do not practise magic.
* Hobbit Monks should not be allowed because hobbits are known for
  eating a lot and monks are known for fasting.
* Hobbit Knights should be allowed because by the end of The Lord of
  the Rings, Merry and Pippin were hobbit knights.  This is the same
  principle by which Droven Rangers are allowed: even if a race/class
  combination is unusual, if there is a specific famous literary
  example that people might want to roleplay, it should be allowed.
* Droven Rogues should be allowed because Drow have many Rogueish
  characteristics like being stealthy and good at using poison.
* Gnomes and Hobbits are both known for being talented thieves, so
  IMHO Gnomish and Hobbit Rogues should be allowed, even though that
  means we need to have neutral Rogues.

The remaining changes mentioned in this post have not been RFEd yet
(this pre-RFE is meant to give everyone a chance to comment first).

Vampiric Barbarians should not be allowed: Dylan says "Vampires have a
refinement that Barbs completely lack."  Similarly, elves are too
refined and civilised to be barbarians, and the "Elven Warrior" type
would be better represented as an Elven Knight.  I don't know enough
about Drow to say whether they also are too civilised, but they
definitely haven't got the thews for it.

Could someone who knows about Gnomes please explain why they are not
allowed to be Monks or Priests?  Also, why are Dwarves forbidden to be
Undead Slayers, when all other races except Vampires are allowed to?
